Subject: [PATCH] Clients icon: swap plain Users glyph for a DiceBear filled
 icon badge
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Plain outline Users icon read as too generic/flat next to the initials
avatars elsewhere in the switcher. Uses DiceBear's `icons` style instead
— a solid glyph on a colored rounded backdrop (the Slack/Discord
default-avatar look), pinned to a fixed seed and one of the same violet
tones used by client initials avatars so it reads as part of the same
color system rather than a one-off.

This sandbox's network policy blocks api.dicebear.com, so the exact
glyph this seed renders hasn't been visually previewed here — swapping
the seed string is a one-line follow-up if it doesn't land.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011PX9qLTKPtXba6ncjAwLyN
